Every job that installs dependencies has a cache: {{ static.jobs_installing }} jobs install with `uv`, and all {{ static.jobs_installing }} run `astral-sh/setup-uv`, which caches by default on GitHub-hosted runners. {{ static.jobs_installing_without_cache | count }} install without a cache. Query: `python -m cidiag query static.jobs`.

Whether the cache is hit can only be read from job logs. In the {{ caches.logs_read }} test-job logs of the {{ caches.sample_runs }} most recent runs on `{{ config.branch }}` that reached a verdict:

